  "text_md": "with the surface aﬃne connection given by\n\n$$\n1 Yab (45)\n$$\n\n$$\nFab + (46)\n$$\n\nand associated torsion tensor F ab deﬁned through\n\n$$\nFab. (47)\n$$\n\nA submanifold Riemann tensor R a bcd can be constructed from γ a ab through the standard form\n\n$$\nR bcd = + Ydf cb 48) da c\n$$\n\nThe boost invariant extrinsic curvature of the submanifold K ab I can be deﬁned from the covariant derivative of the tangential vector through\n\n$$\n= (49) 2 Kab\n$$\n\nand transforming under mass U(1) transformations as\n\n$$\n50) 2 2\n$$\n\nNotice that the covariant derivative D does not act on normal indices I . It is also possible to deﬁne a covariant derivative D that acts on all types of indices. In particular we will ﬁnd that\n\n$$\nWa (51) DaTI DaTI JTJ\n$$\n\nThe tensor ω a I J is called the external rotation tensor and can be interpreted as a SO(d-p) connection, it is deﬁned from the covariant derivative of the normal 1-form\n\n$$\nWa J = (52)\n$$\n\nit is antisymmetric in I, J indices, and transforms under U(1) mass transformations as\n\n$$\n1 (53)\n$$\n\n",
